WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:14.530
Beyond the heavy rain is a rainbow
hageshii ame no mukou kakaru niji wo mita

3
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.170
I'll know the easy answer's a lie
tayasui kotae wa uso dato shiru darou

4
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.880
Vow not to back down to the shouting
dekai koe nanka ni makenai to chikatte

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.630
I need you alone to understand tomorrow
anata hitori ni wakatte hoshii ashita

6
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.770
You gave me the time of my life
yume no youna jikan kureta anata

7
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:51.280
What do I look like? An ANGEL or a DEVIL...
watashi wa dou mieteruno? sorega tenshi ka akuma ka

8
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.240
Beyond the dawn, beyond the dawn
yoake no mukou yoake no mukou

9
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.740
There's so much I want to tell you
hanashitai koto takusan arun da

10
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.540
Filled with love, with love
ai kometa ai kometa

11
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.460
That can't be written down in a letter
tegami ni kakikirenai omoi da

12
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:20.890
A small hand in search of eternity
eien wo sagashita chiisana tenohira

13
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:31.900
Nika?

14
00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.530
That's right, he's my idol.

15
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.070
He appears from the blue 
with laughter and this rythm.

16
00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:53.630
<b>"Kuma's Life"</b>

17
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.130
<b>2 YEARS AGO</b>

18
00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.800
Hey, Bonney!

19
00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.720
Bonney!

20
00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.310
Bonney!

21
00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.600
Jeez!

22
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.770
Don't call me Bonney!

23
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.150
C-ap-ta-in!

24
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.650
Alright, alright, Captain!

25
00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.660
This island right here!
Kumachi must be there!

26
00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.240
What? Are you sure?!

27
00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.910
I'm pretty sure!

28
00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.580
But the thing is, the Marines are also here...

29
00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.290
Dad!

30
00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.210
Let's go, guys!

31
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.040
Disembark!

32
00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.890
It's the Bonney Pirates!

33
00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.720
There's a fleet-wide order for their arrest!

34
00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.100
They say injured elders and children
are left lying in their wake!

35
00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.270
What?!

36
00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.940
Targeting only the weak!
They're absolute trash!

37
00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:55.230
Shoot!

38
00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.440
Get out of my way!

39
00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.030
Age Skewer!

40
00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.370
Kumachi! Where are you?! Show yourself!

41
00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.120
A giant man?
Yes, I just saw him at the edge of town!

42
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.880
- Captain Bonney!
- Someone saw Kumachi!

43
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:14.880
Be right there!

44
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.800
- Where?!
- He said he was that way!

45
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.470
Okay!

46
00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.180
We must not meet.

47
00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.680
Bonney, please understand.

48
00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.430
Don't look for me.

49
00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.980
Why wasn't he there?!

50
00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.730
Look, we're all pirates now, so let's
 take our time searching, Captain.

51
00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.950
Nika, huh?

52
00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.990
Then I wanna look for Nika, too!

53
00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.950
When I see Dad,

54
00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:51.710
he'll be happy if I tell him 
I found Nika on an island somewhere.

55
00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.710
<b>Meanwhile in the East Blue</b>

56
00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.000
Meanwhile in the East Blue...

57
00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:01.130
Gum-Gum...

58
00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.180
...Battle Axe!

59
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.510
After defeating Arlong's crew,
part of the Fish-Man Pirates,

60
00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.770
Straw Hat Luffy rose to 
prominence as a pirate.

61
00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.600
Yay! I got a bounty on my head!

62
00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.520
<b>"Straw Hat Luffy"</b>

63
00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:15.600
<b>Luffy"</b>

64
00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.360
I'm going to Loguetown.

65
00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.110
Loguetown? For what?

66
00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.910
Well... By the way, 
who oversees that area?

67
00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.910
Captain Smoker does.

68
00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:26.990
oker does.

69
00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.330
"Defeated the Arlong Pirates"

70
00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:31.330
Jinbe, Jinbe!
Guess whose little brother he is!

71
00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.620
The answer is my little brother!

72
00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:39.300
What?! The kid who beat 
the Arlong Pirates is your brother?!

73
00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.300
It's funny, Dragon...

74
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.130
Both of our children became pirates...

75
00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.220
These are the ironclad laws
 of piratey behavior!

76
00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.680
Plunder whatever you want!

77
00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.640
Plunder!

78
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.930
Only from bad guys!

79
00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.480
Don't help people!

80
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.690
Don't!

81
00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.900
Unless they need it!

82
00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.230
Like this?

83
00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:04.450
That's it!
I think that's how you wear lipstick.

84
00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.070
Yes! I'm all grown-up!

85
00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:10.910
If I don't put something on my cheek,
Dad might not recognize me.

86
00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:11.830
And...

87
00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.950
...I should become famous!

88
00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.330
Then I'm sure he'll notice me!

89
00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.750
Right, Dad?

90
00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.420
<b>Egghead, 
New World</b>

91
00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.300
I find this creepy.

92
00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.760
I'm not surprised.

93
00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.720
Clone soldier production is going
 well, just like your modifications.

94
00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:37.440
Anyway, have you heard about the boy who
 declared war against the World Government?

95
00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.400
Shoot down that flag.

96
00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:40.310
Roger.

97
00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.230
What?! He's Dragon's son?!

98
00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:48.070
You'll see my memories anyway,
so there's no point in hiding it from you.

99
00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:52.700
Coincidence or not, he also defies the Government with his rubber powers.

100
00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.700
He is exactly like Nika, my hero.

101
00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:57.540
You're right.

102
00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.330
Gum-Gum...

103
00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.380
...Giant Jet Shell!

104
00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:10.550
<b>Thriller Bark, 
Grand Line</b>
My mission is to exterminate every single one of you, but...

105
00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:14.310
I want you to bring me Straw Hat Luffy's head.

106
00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.020
As long as they have him, the Government won't mind.

107
00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.980
Betray our comrade...?!

108
00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:22.940
We refuse!

109
00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.320
Such a shame.

110
00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.610
Ursa Shock!

111
00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.320
Then, go ahead and take it...

112
00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.280
But not his head!

113
00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:38.540
I beg you to take my life instead of his!

114
00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.540
Luffy's the man who is gonna
 be the Pirate King!

115
00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.840
If you really intend to take his place,

116
00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.920
then you must literally share his suffering.

117
00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.510
This would even knock me unconscious.

118
00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.940
He has good friends.

119
00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:03.940
As expected from your son,

120
00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:04.730
Dragon.

121
00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.860
Ring, ring, ring... Clank.

122
00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.780
Seven Warlords, mandatory summons!

123
00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.700
Refuse, and your title will be revoked!

124
00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:15.530
Don't be so dramatic. What's this about?

125
00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:20.710
The bannerman of the new generation,
Portgas D. Ace's public execution is now set.

126
00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:25.090
That means there will be war
with the Whitebeard Pirates!

127
00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.800
War with Whitebeard?

128
00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.380
I'll definitely be there in time.

129
00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.970
<b>Sabaody Archipelago</b>

130
00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:32.970
Isn't the food here yet?!

131
00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.930
We're running out of it!

132
00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.890
Get me more pizza!

133
00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:41.350
It seems they're cooking it as
 fast as they can, Captain.

134
00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.190
They won't make it in time, at this rate!

135
00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.400
Captain! If you make a scene,
the Marines will...

136
00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.780
This will be the last time I see her.

137
00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.860
She's become quite a tough pirate...

138
00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.410
Bonney.

139
00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.660
A pirate struck a Celestial Dragon!

140
00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.170
"Human Shop"?!

141
00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.130
Who did what to a Celestial Dragon?!

142
00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:09.800
That's a global taboo.

143
00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.420
And it's close to Marine Headquarters.

144
00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.140
It's an act of suicide!

145
00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.230
It's the Straw Hats again!

146
00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:34.150
Are they trying to protect
a Fish-Man and a Mermaid?!

147
00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.870
Look, Straw Hat Luffy.

148
00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:45.920
This is probably an act of treason...

149
00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.750
...that no one has managed to pull off...

150
00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.090
...in many centuries!

151
00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.970
Wait, PX-1.

152
00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.020
Dragon.

153
00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:07.650
Iva-chan.

154
00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.190
Forgive me for disappearing
without a word.

155
00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:24.200
As a mark of my existence,
I'll quietly leave behind…

156
00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:27.830
...Bonney

157
00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:31.920
and this boy's future.

158
00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:44.390
I couldn't even...

159
00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.940
...save a single one of my friends!

160
00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.730
That is not true.

161
00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:55.070
This is just the level of the New World.

162
00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.070
It is still too soon for your crew.

163
00:09:58.410 --> 00:09:59.530
Don't come here yet.

164
00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.120
One day in the future...

165
00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.330
...you will be the man who saves the world.

166
00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.760
A self-destruct switch?!

167
00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.260
How much do you fear Kuma?!

168
00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:21.470
You turned him into a deadly human weapon.

169
00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.930
You're at the top of the authority hierarchy!

170
00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.770
But if he goes berserk
when we are out of command range,

171
00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.650
who will stop him and how?

172
00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:30.600
Well...

173
00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:34.570
Cease this insolence.
You are a paltry hired scientist.

174
00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:39.030
Then, in exchange for installing that into him,
let him keep a bit of his free will!

175
00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:43.450
I've invented a brain circuit
that can toggle between personalities!

176
00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:45.120
If you let me try it...

177
00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.330
I gave you an order, Vegapunk.

178
00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.170
You will not leave him any free will!

179
00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:54.290
I am a scientist myself.
You cannot trick me.

180
00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.590
But then Kuma

181
00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.300
and Bonney will never be able to meet again...!

182
00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.510
Clank.

183
00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.520
I appreciate the sentiment, Vegapunk.

184
00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:11.230
What?! There's no way
you could hear that conversation.

185
00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.650
Who was it who gave me superhuman hearing?

186
00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:22.320
"Justice"

187
00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:29.290
Okay!
Today is the day you lose your free will.

188
00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:33.290
I've only known you for two years,
but we had so much fun!

189
00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:35.710
We did.

190
00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:40.420
I think your first mission will be
a fight against the Whitebeard Pirates.

191
00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.180
They've ordered a mass deployment 
of clone soldiers.

192
00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:47.850
I want you to program me a mission
after that.

193
00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:52.560
Protecting the Straw Hats' ship?!

194
00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:57.020
Until one of their crew comes back,
I want to protect their home.

195
00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:00.990
I will not be around to see
their growth anymore, but...

196
00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:04.450
What are you expecting from that kid?

197
00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:08.700
Something in his actions shakes
 the very core of my being.

198
00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.660
Nika is merely a legend.

199
00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.210
But I instilled into Bonney...

200
00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:20.050
...stories of a warrior who rides the rhythm
 of liberation and brings smiles to all.

201
00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:24.590
If there is a hero
who will change this world drastically...

202
00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:28.560
I believe it'll be him.

203
00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.560
A revolutionary betting on a pirate...

204
00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.770
You've chosen quite a dark horse.

205
00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:38.520
That contradiction is proof of your humanity.

206
00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:42.490
Now, provide me materials
for my scientific research.

207
00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:43.990
We had a deal.

208
00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.790
When you push them out of you,
do you lose your memories?

209
00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.580
No, it's like a copy.

210
00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.460
But it'll vanish when it's touched.

211
00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:58.500
That's fine. I created a system
that allows me to study it from a distance.

212
00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.710
Put it right there.

213
00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.920
Now, this will be quick.

214
00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.930
This is just a clinical process.
I'm a scientist.

215
00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:09.760
So this is...

216
00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.430
...my life...

217
00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.860
How many people have I troubled?

218
00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:20.270
Troubling others!

219
00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.980
Indeed, to live is to cause others trouble!

220
00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:10.120
Kumachi, when did you become a slave?

221
00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:12.830
When I was four.

222
00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.290
Me too!

223
00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.500
Kumachi!

224
00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:20.670
Since I'm four years older than you,
I have to feed you!

225
00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.710
Kumachi!

226
00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:31.090
Kumachi!

227
00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.150
Kumachi! Kumachi!

228
00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.080
Kumachi!

229
00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.370
I'm full!

230
00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.290
I'm full...!

231
00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.040
I'm... full...

232
00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.970
I'm so happy.

233
00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.890
Kumachi...

234
00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.060
I'll always...

235
00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:17.720
...always...

236
00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.060
...love you.

237
00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:37.870
Don't worry, Ginny.

238
00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:40.410
I'll raise your daughter.

239
00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.420
Daddy!

240
00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.790
Dad!

241
00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.630
Daddy!

242
00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.340
Dad!

243
00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.180
Those punks...

244
00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:02.060
...made fun of the stones on my face!

245
00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.350
Is it that weird?

246
00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.650
But it's a disease. I can't help it.

247
00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:11.240
I'm going to be honest with you.
Your daughter...

248
00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.610
...has five years at most to live.

249
00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.990
She won't live to see her tenth birthday.

250
00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:20.870
Your mother's dead...

251
00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.790
She should be in heaven by now.

252
00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.960
Hey, Kuma. You're strong.

253
00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:32.300
Endure! Endure and survive!

254
00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:35.970
Why? I think I'd be better off dead too...

255
00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.760
The Warrior of Liberation will come!

256
00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.810
He'll come to save you!

257
00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.270
Who is that?

258
00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.560
I can't take it anymore...

259
00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.900
I can't take it!

260
00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.900
I don't want to...

261
00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.410
...lose anyone else!

262
00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:03.790
Nika?

263
00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.420
That's right, he's my idol.

264
00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.540
Will he come and free me, too?!

265
00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.260
The mass of pain and suffering...

266
00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.720
...won't just disappear
until someone accepts it.

267
00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:29.730
Your hands liberated people.

268
00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.230
Those are the Hands of Liberation!

269
00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:41.580
Thank you.

270
00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:46.960
If Bonney gets well,

271
00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.170
I will gladly accept...

272
00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.170
"Dad"

273
00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:52.920
...any fate!

274
00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.340
Nika, the Sun God!

275
00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:59.930
One day, he'll come and take you out...

276
00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.850
...under the sun, to the freedom of the sea!

277
00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:04.770
Are you sure?

278
00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:05.810
Yes.

279
00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.190
I'm sure.

280
00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:12.020
I'll be cured in a year and get to go outside!

281
00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:16.780
Next time we meet, let's be out on the sea,
watching the horizon together.

282
00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:20.450
Can't wait!
And I wanna go on many trips!

283
00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:29.170
Bonney.

284
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.170
Ever since I was a child,

285
00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:40.590
I wanted to be a hero who could save the downtrodden and suffering.

286
00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:00.950
Kuma!

287
00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.530
Kumachi!

288
00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:08.870
Kuma!

289
00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:10.540
Kuma!

290
00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.420
Kumachi!

291
00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:19.670
Daddy!

292
00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:23.930
It's curable!

293
00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:30.390
Dad!

294
00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.100
I'm so glad!

295
00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:38.940
Thank you!

296
00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.460
Troubling others!

297
00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:56.250
Indeed, to live is to cause others trouble!

298
00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:01.590
Your death will be trouble...

299
00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:04.050
...for everyone who's ever loved you!

300
00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:05.760
Listen to me, Kuma.

301
00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:09.020
You are the hero...

302
00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:11.640
For Bonney!

303
00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:13.940
And for us all!

304
00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:15.810
Thank you.

305
00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.650
Say, Vegapunk...

306
00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:23.360
Yes, I already know.

307
00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:27.830
Nika?

308
00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.120
That's right, he's my idol.

309
00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:35.380
Will he come and free me, too?!

310
00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.460
Of course!

311
00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.890
Thank you...

312
00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:55.730
...for saving Bonney.

313
00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:02.150
Could you tell her this when you see her?

314
00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:10.330
I wish her a happy...

315
00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:15.750
...tenth birthday.

316
00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:37.020
I can't protect anyone again
mata daremo mamorenai no

317
00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.820
It's my fault that the voice is fading away
kiekakaru koe wa boku no sei

318
00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.110
I don't even have time to look down
utsumuku hima mo nai no

319
00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.700
Gravel marks on my palms
tenohira ni tsuku jari no ato

320
00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.080
Start moving again, my ship
mata ugokidase boku no fune yo

321
00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:55.580
Though I can't fly in the broad sky
hiroi sora wa tobenai kedo

322
00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:01.460
I can light up the deep sea
fukai umi wa teraseru kara

323
00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.420
We
bokura wa

324
00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:04.920
EVERYDAY owarenai
EVERYDAY, can't let this be the end

325
00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:07.550
EVERYDAY makerenai
EVERYDAY, can't be defeated

326
00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:11.310
We have something here to protect
mamoru mono ga koko niwa aru

327
00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:13.850
This may not be what I expected
yosou chigai kamo?

328
00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.560
But we can't stop now
tomarenai yo mou

329
00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:21.860
We go on, sharing loneliness
kodoku wo ima wakeai susumu

330
00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:24.610
Don't be afraid
ojikedukuna yo

331
00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:28.570
I'm not the same person I was that day
ano hi no boku to chigau kara

332
00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:32.030
No one can stand in my way
dare nimo jama dekinai yo

333
00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:33.660
Now, move aside
saa doite

334
00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:36.250
Conquer the world, believe in the future
sekai wo seishite mirai wo shinjite

335
00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:38.830
Count up the nights
ikutsu mono yoru kazoete

336
00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:41.540
What did you see? What did you learn?
nani wo mite nani wo shitte

337
00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:44.550
To realize what was important
taisetsu na koto ni kiduita no
